  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Adding value to coffee through a dry mill and improving quality to increase market access</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cooperativa de Servicios Mltiples San Rafael Inc. (Cooperativa San Rafael) a farmer cooperative in Peralta Azua plans to work with farmers to improve the quality of their processed coffee so that they can access niche markets. It will install a centralized dry mill; train farmers to apply organic practices and sort and classify beans; and provide materials and financing to improve plantations; open a cooperative store selling basic goods; and start a seed bank. Approximately 250 farmers will directly benefit and another 1250 residents of Peralta will benefit indirectly.</narrative>
  </description>
